Bugfix: A connection hiccup no longer reloads the page during an upload

Any background request of the web interface that failed without a response
(status 0) - the notifications poll every 30 seconds, for example - made the
global error handler reload the page after five seconds. A running upload was
lost with it; for a file of several gigabytes that meant hours of uploading.
While an upload is in progress the page now stays: the upload resumes after
its own failures, and the background requests retry by themselves. Lost
sessions (401) and redirects still reload the page as before.
